<bx:script>
	request.pageTitle = "GC pressure";
	running = application.scenarios.isRunning( "gc" );
	request.lookAt = [
		"Console > System: GC count and total GC time climb quickly while heap stays flat (churn, not a leak).",
		"Compare with Memory growth, where heap climbs and stays up.",
		"Ask Lensy about garbage collection pressure."
	];
</bx:script>
<bx:include template="/includes/header.bxm" />
<bx:output>
<h1>GC pressure</h1>
<p>A thread allocates and drops 8 MB arrays in a tight loop for 60 seconds. Nothing is kept, but the collector never rests.</p>
<p>State: <span class="pill #running ? 'on' : ''#">#running ? application.scenarios.detail( "gc" ) : "idle"#</span></p>
<p>
	<a class="btn go" href="/control.bxm?action=start&id=gc&seconds=60&return=/runtime/gc-pressure.bxm">Start (60 s)</a>
	<a class="btn reset" href="/control.bxm?action=reset&id=gc&return=/runtime/gc-pressure.bxm">Reset</a>
</p>
</bx:output>
<bx:include template="/includes/footer.bxm" />
